    "limits": "Run logs are local and git-ignored; a matching hash establishes spec identity, not a run. The first four evidence entries are historical receipts whose runtime and runner inputs, such as editable-dom-runtime.ts, model-input-strategy.ts and playwright.config.ts, changed after they ran. The useCombobox and combobox browser specs changed after the closure record, and their final runs exist only in local logs. IME proof is synthetic Chromium CDP composition only: physical desktop and mobile IME, Android taps during composition and WebKit's confirming Enter on a real IME are missing, and Playwright WebKit is not Safari. Under emulated Android a blur that commits a composition leaves Plite's caret past the committed text. The native owner has not reviewed the public settleInput or its fallback. Autocomplete inside owned content roots is not built. Two views of one document, a live Copilot model beside Mention, screen-reader navigation, the element read-only recheck in complete, and migration of named roots and of inputs with meaningful children have no case. isAnotherEditorFocused reads data-editor attributes until Plite reports which Editable holds a shared selection. The key-to-paint contract passed only on the development server, with about 2 ms of per-run noise. pnpm check did not run because the tree held other sessions' changes. The October 3 reruns ran in a working checkout that held other sessions' uncommitted edits; their logs are local and their inputs were not hashed. The registry install proof fails on these bytes on DnD registry types and stops before its later steps. Hard law 5 has known violations: string data pasted, yanked, dropped or labeled a replacement and inserted at a collapsed caret passes the typing-check helper, a real replacement range is unverified, and an Android keyboard-clipboard paste arrives as insertText."
